course: dictionary
lesson: 6229
title: Mm: a tiny measure and a tasty sound
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Mm is a short way to write millimetre, which is a very tiny unit of length. Ten millimetres make one centimetre, so a millimetre is a tenth of a centimetre. Small things like pencil leads, raindrops and insects are measured in mm.
explain: «A squash ball is about 40 mm across.» The mm after the number tells you the unit, so 40 mm means forty millimetres. Look for the number and the unit together to understand the size.
explain: Mmm, with an extra m, is a different kind of word. It is a sound people make to say yes, to think, or to say food is tasty. Context helps you tell them apart: a unit comes after a number, while «Mmm!» stands alone in a sentence.
fact: Mm means millimetre, a very small unit of length.
fact: There are 10 millimetres in 1 centimetre.
fact: «The Goliath frog of West Africa can be about 32 cm long, while the smallest frogs are under 8 mm long.»
fact: «Mmm» is a sound people make to say yes, to think, or to say food is tasty.
fact: «A desert is a place where very little rain or snow falls, usually less than about 250 mm a year.»
exercise: «The smallest frogs are under 8 mm long.» What does mm mean here? | Minute | Mile | *Millimetre | Mountain
exercise: Ella takes a bite and says, «Mmm!» with a big smile. What does it show? | *The food tastes good | She is angry | Something is cold | She is counting
exercise: How many millimetres are in one centimetre? | 5 | *10 | 100 | 1
test: «A desert is a place where very little rain falls, usually less than about 250 mm a year.» What does this tell you about deserts? | *Deserts can be cold as well as hot, because they get very little rain | Deserts are only sandy | Deserts are always hot | Deserts have a lot of rain
test: In «A squash ball is about 40 mm across», what kind of word is mm? | A type of rain | *A short way of writing millimetre | A sound people make | A famous frog
exam: Which is longer, the Goliath frog at about 32 cm or the smallest frogs under 8 mm? | The smallest frogs under 8 mm | Neither, they are the same length | *The Goliath frog at about 32 cm | They cannot be compared
